</form><p class="hint">A is the earlier candle; B is the later candle. “L:A” means A owns the lowest wick. BO&lt;AC means B open is below A close. Equality is recorded separately. Identical price levels can have multiple OHLC names.</p>
<p class="note">Boundaries are the full A/B pair’s lowest and highest wicks. Eligibility uses only information available before entry, starting after candle B—even during swing confirmation. Later breakouts stay in the denominator. A boundary break and reaction target in one candle counts as boundary-first. No observed percentage guarantees future outcomes.</p></section>
