<section><h2>What is being measured?</h2><p><strong>Contained reaction:</strong> reaching the selected point distance before either original boundary breaks. <strong>Trade result:</strong> BUY stop one tick below the pair low; SELL stop one tick above the pair high, with the selected target. A trade can profit after leaving the original range, so these rates are deliberately separate.</p>
<p>120 one-minute bars to revisit; 30 continuous bars including entry for each observation. Only complete windows are scored. NQ $20/point, one contract, $5 round-trip cost sensitivity. Intrabar order is unknown: stop first when stop and target both touch; entry-bar targets require a close at/beyond target. Overlapping trials are alternative simulations, not portfolio returns. Annual breakdowns are descriptive; these data have already been explored and are not an untouched validation set.</p>
<p>Authenticated API: <code>level-revisit-api.php?resource=manifest</code>, <code>rankings</code>, <code>rule&amp;id=…</code>, <code>example&amp;id=…&amp;example=0</code>. Uses your existing HTTPS bearer API key (or X-Api-Token header). Read-only full-dataset results; the selected TP changes the displayed outcome, not the underlying audit.</p></section></main>
